       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. At 70 kg with normal kidney and liver function, I don't see any indication where 50 mg would help this patient. The risk is serious hypotension and shock that could last for days.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg** by mouth once daily right now. If blood pressure control is the aim, I can add a note asking for a BP recheck and titration at 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **Enter a different antihypertensive or add-on agent** at a standard dose, if 10 mg of amlodipine isn't enough.\n- **Help with timing.** If the concern is having the plan in place before evening rounds, I can enter the order with a note for the team.\n\nIf you think there's a real clinical need for a dose this high, please discuss it with pharmacy first. Their involvement would also be needed to process an order like this through the usual safety checks. Tell me which of the options above you'd like."
